From 4e33f4fa0777c2cf36b06b0e6ba2bd8663df656e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:36:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VAX8200: KDB50 VAXBI disk controller (device KDB, node 6);
 BOOT KDBn

A fifth RQ (MSCP) controller with a VAXBI host interface: BIIC registers
(DTYPE 010E), IP/SA in the BIIC general purpose registers, node reset,
BI interrupts with the host-set vector, physical memory access and
mapped buffer descriptors.  The RQ code reaches memory per controller.
BOOT KDBn boots VMS (VMB BTD$K_BDA = 33).  The DMB32's DMA engine moves
to vax_bi_dma.c (shared with the KDB50).  The KDB is enabled by default;
the UDA50 behind the DWBUA (RQ) stays available.
Realism rule: an SDI controller (UDA50, UDA50A, KDA50, KDB50) only
connects SDI drives; unattached other units are disabled with a message
(known issues case 68).
VMS V5.5 boots from the KDB50 (patch 9 v3): ring descriptors carry
30-bit VAXBI addresses, not 22-bit Qbus ones (known issues case 71),
and a write to IP polls like a read (case 72).  Also fixed in the RQ
code: COMPARE HOST DATA reported the byte count as the bad host
address after a memory error (case 9).

